    "# 06 - Multiclass Classification (Iris)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Section:** ANNs | **Prereqs:** `ANNs/NumNodes` | **Next:** `ANNs/DepthVsBreadth.ipynb`\n",
    "\n",
    "The first model on real data: 150 flowers, 4 measurements, 3 species. Going from\n",
    "2 classes to 3 changes three things and nothing else.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Binary | Multiclass |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Output units | 1 | one per class (3) |\n",
    "| Final activation | `Sigmoid` | none - see below |\n",
    "| Loss | `BCELoss` | `CrossEntropyLoss` |\n",
    "| Labels | float 0.0/1.0 | **int64** class indices |\n",
    "| Prediction | `out > 0.5` | `argmax(out, axis=1)` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**The rule people get wrong:** `nn.CrossEntropyLoss` applies `log_softmax`\n",
    "itself, so the model must output **raw logits**. Adding a `Softmax` layer before\n",
    "it is the single most common PyTorch bug - it trains, badly, and quietly."
   ]
  },
